  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Why IaC and Declarative vs Imperative",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Why IaC and Declarative vs Imperative",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What IaC Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Infra as ==version-controlled text files==",
                "{green:Reproducible} environments",
                "{blue:Reviewable} in PRs",
                "{purple:Auditable} Git history",
                "Not built by clicking in a console"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Declarative vs Imperative",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Declarative",
                "Imperative"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Tools",
                  "Terraform, CloudFormation",
                  "bash + CLI, SDK scripts"
                ],
                [
                  "You write",
                  "Desired **end state**",
                  "Exact **ordered steps**"
                ],
                [
                  "Free",
                  "Diffs, ordering, destroy",
                  "Full control, flexibility"
                ],
                [
                  "Hand-write",
                  "Nothing",
                  "Ordering, errors, cleanup"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Idempotent== = re-running a config changes nothing if reality already matches",
                "Imperative `create` script run twice → {red:fails or duplicates}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Desired state",
                    "sub": "your config",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Diff",
                    "sub": "vs reality",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Order",
                    "sub": "dependencies",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Apply",
                    "sub": "changes only",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why declarative?** Diffs, ordering, destroy come free; PR-reviewable",
                "**Idempotent?** Re-run changes nothing if reality matches",
                "**Imperative still right?** One-off tasks, glue steps"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Declarative = ==what== you want; imperative = **how** to get there."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Providers and Resources",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Providers and Resources",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Providers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Provider== = plugin turning HCL into API calls",
                "Declared in `required_providers`: ==source== + version",
                "`terraform init` downloads it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "hcl",
              "lines": [
                "terraform {",
                "  required_providers {",
                "    aws = {",
                "      source  = \"hashicorp/aws\"",
                "      version = \"~> 5.0\"",
                "    }",
                "  }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Resources and Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "hcl",
              "lines": [
                "resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"logs\" {",
                "  bucket = \"my-logs\"",
                "}",
                "resource \"aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block\" \"p\" {",
                "  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.logs.id",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "first address: aws_s3_bucket.logs"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Type + local name = ==address==, unique per config",
                "A reference makes an ==implicit dependency==",
                "`depends_on` only for ==hidden== dependencies"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Data, Inputs, Outputs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "resource",
                "data"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Block",
                  "`resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"logs\"`",
                  "`data \"aws_ami\" \"ubuntu\"`"
                ],
                [
                  "Does",
                  "creates and manages",
                  "only reads existing"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`variable` takes inputs, `output` exposes values: ==reusable== config"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**init downloads?** Provider plugins",
                "**Resource vs data?** Manages vs only reads",
                "**Order?** Reference graph; `depends_on` for hidden links"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "State, Plan and Apply",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "State, Plan and Apply",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What State Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==terraform.tfstate== maps each resource address to its real-world ID and attributes",
                "Terraform diffs {blue:config} vs {purple:state} vs {green:refreshed reality}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Plan and Apply",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`terraform plan` is a ==read-only== preview; `terraform apply` executes it",
                "A saved plan applies **exactly** what was reviewed: the safe pattern for CI"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Symbol",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:+}",
                  "create"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:~}",
                  "update in place"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:-/+}",
                  "replace: destroy, then create"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:-}",
                  "destroy"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "terraform plan -out=tfplan",
                "terraform apply tfplan"
              ],
              "note": "applies the reviewed plan, nothing newer"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Remote Backend",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Shares state across a team and ==locks== it: no two applies at once",
                "S3: `use_lockfile = true` replaces the deprecated DynamoDB lock",
                "Or HCP Terraform, formerly Terraform Cloud"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "State rules",
              "items": [
                "Never hand-edit it or commit it to Git",
                "May hold secrets in plaintext: encrypt, restrict access"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "takeaway",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "**No hand-edit or Git?** Plaintext secrets, and edits desync state from reality. **Locking?** Stops two concurrent applies. **-/+ ?** Destroy first: risk to a database or disk."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Everyday Terraform Commands",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Everyday Terraform Commands",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Core Loop",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "init",
                    "sub": "providers, backend",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fmt",
                    "sub": "format files",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "validate",
                    "sub": "syntax, types, no API",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "plan",
                    "sub": "preview",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "apply",
                    "sub": "execute",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`terraform destroy` removes ==everything in state==",
                "`apply -target=ADDR` limits scope: {red:emergencies only}, not routine"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. State and Import",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`state list`",
                  "lists addresses in state"
                ],
                [
                  "`state show ADDR`",
                  "shows one resource's attributes"
                ],
                [
                  "`state rm ADDR`",
                  "stops managing, ==no delete=="
                ],
                [
                  "`state mv OLD NEW`",
                  "renames address, ==no recreate=="
                ],
                [
                  "`import ADDR ID`",
                  "adopts an existing resource"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Import",
              "text": "It writes state only. You must write the matching ==resource block== yourself."
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "hcl",
              "lines": [
                "import {",
                "  to = aws_s3_bucket.logs",
                "  id = \"my-logs\"",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "block form of: terraform import aws_s3_bucket.logs my-logs"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Be ready to answer",
              "items": [
                "**validate vs plan?** validate checks syntax offline; plan diffs config against state",
                "**Rename without destroying?** `state mv OLD NEW`, then rename in config",
                "**Adopt a manual resource?** write its resource block, then `import ADDR ID`"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Drift, Environments and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Drift, Environments and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Drift",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Console edit",
                    "sub": "outside Terraform",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "plan",
                    "sub": "refreshes, shows diff",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "apply",
                    "sub": "reverts to config",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`apply -refresh-only` ==records== reality in state, resources untouched",
                "`plan -refresh-only` only __previews__ that update"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Environments",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setup",
                "State",
                "Fit"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Directory per env",
                  "separate",
                  "prod"
                ],
                [
                  "Module + `-var-file=prod.tfvars`",
                  "separate",
                  "prod"
                ],
                [
                  "Workspaces",
                  "shared backend + config",
                  "light only"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Prod",
              "text": "Use ==separate state and backends==. A wrong selected workspace applies to prod."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Committing `tfstate` or secrets",
                "`apply` without reading the plan",
                "Unpinned provider versions",
                "One giant state file",
                "Hand edits in the console"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Detect and fix drift?** `plan` shows it; `apply` reverts it, or update config to keep it",
                "**Workspaces vs directories?** Workspaces share a backend; directories isolate state",
                "**Avoid wrong-env prod apply?** Separate backend, `-var-file`, read the plan"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Terraform and IaC Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Terraform and IaC Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Mental Model",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Piece",
                "Role"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Config**",
                  "==desired state==, declarative and idempotent"
                ],
                [
                  "**State**",
                  "what Terraform ==believes exists=="
                ],
                [
                  "**Plan**",
                  "the ==diff== between them"
                ],
                [
                  "**Apply**",
                  "==converge== reality to config"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Edit .tf",
                    "sub": "config",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Plan",
                    "sub": "lock, refresh, diff",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Apply tfplan",
                    "sub": "change resource",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "State saved",
                    "sub": "unlock",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Workflow",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "terraform init",
                "terraform fmt",
                "terraform validate",
                "terraform plan -out=tfplan",
                "terraform apply tfplan",
                "terraform destroy"
              ],
              "note": "destroy tears down everything in state"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Plan Symbols",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Symbol",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`+`",
                  "{green:create}"
                ],
                [
                  "`~`",
                  "update in place"
                ],
                [
                  "`-`",
                  "{red:destroy}"
                ],
                [
                  "`-/+`",
                  "{red:replace}: destroy, then create"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. State Tools",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`state list` and `state show ADDR` inspect state",
                "`state rm` stops managing; `state mv` renames, no recreate",
                "`import ADDR ID` adopts a resource; write its block yourself",
                "`plan -refresh-only` previews drift; `apply -refresh-only` records it",
                "Team: remote backend with ==locking== (S3 `use_lockfile = true`, HCP Terraform)"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pause on -/+",
              "text": "A replace on a ==database or disk== destroys data. Read the plan before you apply."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "The plan shows `-/+ aws_db_instance.main`. What happens on apply?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It ==destroys, then creates== the database, so the data is lost",
                "Find the attribute that forces replacement and snapshot first"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Someone edits a security group in the console. What do `plan` and `apply` do?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Plan shows `~` update back to the config; apply ==reverts the edit==",
                "To keep the edit: `apply -refresh-only` records it in state, then update the config"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You rename the block `logs` to `audit` in the .tf file. What does plan show, and how do you avoid it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`-` destroy logs and `+` create audit, because state still holds the old address",
                "Run `terraform state mv aws_s3_bucket.logs aws_s3_bucket.audit` first"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}